number is a measurement, not a proxy\",\"A matrix whose every number carries its protocol\"],\"dependencies\":[],\"goal\":\"Write bench/fn-stream-client.py and bench/run-matrix.sh per spec claims 6.2 and 6.3 (specs/flashnext/spec.md#r6). The client measures per-request time-to-first-token client-side AND scrapes the server metrics endpoint to separate scheduler queue wait from prompt processing — the reference harness's client published a prefill column that duplicated its first-token column (specs/flashnext/evidence/nix-strix-halo.md section 4.4); ours must not. Emit CSV with explicit column semantics in a header comment, plus a sha256 fingerprint of every completion's token ids. run-matrix.sh: arms interleaved A-B-B-A, three loads per arm, medians reported, depth series 0, 10240, 102400 tokens, speculative decoding on and off arms, results committed under results/ and a bench.json receipt {loads_per_arm, counterbalanced:true, arms, fingerprints}. Add tests/test_bench_client.py: feed the client parser a fixture with known queue and processing times and assert the two columns separate them. Boundaries: touch only bench/ and tests/.\",\"id\":\"bench-harness\",\"kind\":\"implementation\",\"readFirst\":{\"specSections\":[\"specs/flashnext/spec.md#r6\",\"specs/flashnext/evidence/nix-strix-halo.md\"],\"styleReferences\":[\"scripts/receipts-verify.py\"]},\"revision\":\"sha256:3a8882e61c9b2ce9ef7a7904e06778f0284df952e4a68deb4f8e6e1caba1a225\",\"title\":\"Measurement harness: honest client and counterbalanced matrix\"},\"workspace\":{\"baseRev\":\"b474021c40d16a6bd0fce9ac2b9002b4e6538cc4\",\"branch\":\"tally-work/flashnext-70bb1f7ebb6a/bench-harness\",\"conflictDomains\":[\"bench\",\"tests\"],\"publishBranch\":\"tally/flashnext-campaign-01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/bench-harness-3a8882e61c9b2ce9\",\"taskId\":\"bench-harness\",\"worktreePath\":\"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/70bb1f7ebb6a/bench-harness\"},\"steering\":{\"channel\":\"locally-authorized-snapshot\",\"authorizedComments\":[{\"author\":\"uid:1000\",\"body\":\"PRE-DISPATCH STEER (overseer, community intel — flashnext#4, no scope change). Multi-sequence QSA gather on gfx1151 HIP has documented wrong-output/crash behavior in the llama.cpp stack. Our vLLM code path differs, but harden the matrix against it: (1) the bench matrix MUST record the concurrency (number of in-flight sequences) per arm in its output rows; (2) if any token fingerprint diverges across runs of the same arm, the harness must byte-compare a serial (concurrency=1) replay of that arm before its numbers are trusted — flag the arm as suspect in the output rather than averaging over the divergence. Fingerprint divergence at concurrency>1 with a clean serial replay is the QSA-gather signature; record it, do not paper over it.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-29T06:28:32.507Z\",\"id\":3,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-08-29T06:28:32.507Z\",\"url\":\"local://campaign/01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/steering/3\"}],\"attemptReceipt\":{\"lateRecheckCommentIds\":[],\"preparedCommentIds\":[3],\"recheckTruncated\":false,\"rechecked\":true,\"source\":{\"kind\":\"local-jsonl\",\"path\":\"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/steering/01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/steering-v1.jsonl\",\"preparedCursor\":4,\"recheckedCursor\":4,\"registrationId\":\"01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae\"}},\"machineDiagnoses\":[],\"machineOutcomes\":[]}}"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787990011970}}
