ashnext/evidence/nix-strix-halo.md`\n- Style references: `scripts/receipts-verify.py`\n\n**Steering (authorized comments):**\nFrom the overseer (community intelligence — flashnext#4):\n- Multi-sequence QSA gather on gfx1151 HIP has documented wrong-output/crash behavior in the llama.cpp stack\n- Our vLLM code path is different, but harden the matrix against this:\n  1. The bench matrix MUST record the concurrency (number of in-flight sequences) per arm on output rows\n  2. If any token fingerprint diverges across runs of the same arm, the harness must byte-compare a serial (concurrency=1) replay of that arm before trusting the numbers — rather than averaging across the divergence, flag that arm as suspect in the output\n  - Fingerprint divergence at concurrency>1 combined with clean serial replay is the QSA-gather signature. Record it, don't paper over it.\n\n**Workspace:**\n- baseRev: `b474021c40d16a6bd0fce9ac2b9002b4e6538cc4`\n- branch: `tally-work/flashnext-70bb1f7ebb6a/bench-harness`\n- publishBranch: `tally/flashnext-campaign-01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/bench-harness-3a8882e61c9b2ce9`\n- worktreePath: current directory\n\nLet me start by reading the spec sections and style references. I'll also look at the existing structure. Let me read the spec first.\n\nSince this is a stateless reconciliation attempt, I should inspect the assigned lane and preserve any task work that already exists. Let me check whether bench/ or tests/ already has work in them.\n\nI'll start by exploring.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"This is a spec-build task for a measurement harness. Let me read the cited spec sections, style references, and inspect the current state of the worktree.\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_54080c28a854425889f248dc","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/70bb1f7ebb6a/bench-harness\necho \"=== git status ===\"; git status 2>&1 | head -20\necho \"=== git br