{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The dataclass processing fails because the module isn't registered in sys.modules when exec_module runs. The dataclass decorator in Python 3.14 looks up `sys.modules[cls.__module__]`. Since we load via importlib without registering, `cls.__module__` is \"fn_stream_client\" but it's not in sys.modules.\n\nTwo fixes:\n1. In the test loader, register the module in sys.modules before exec_module. But that changes the test loader; other tests (test_instruments) load modules with dataclasses? Let me check — test_instruments loads fn_offload_batch which probably doesn't use dataclasses, so it didn't hit this. \n2. Avoid dataclasses in the client, or register the module.\n\nThe cleanest fix that keeps the client robust regardless of how it's loaded: register the module in sys.modules in the test loader. But if someone else loads the client differently, dataclasses would still fail. Actually, the client is meant to be run as a script (`python3 bench/fn-stream-client.py`), where `__name__ == \"__main__\"` and it IS in sys.modules. The dataclass issue only arises when loaded via importlib without registration.\n\nThe standard fix in the loader: add `sys.modules[spec.name] = mod` before `spec.loader.exec_module(mod)`. Let me check how test_instruments does it — it does NOT register. But fn_offload_batch doesn't use dataclasses, so no problem.\n\nI have two options:\nA. Fix the test loader to register the module in sys.modules.\nB. Avoid dataclasses in the client (use plain classes or namedtuple).\n\nOption A is cleaner and keeps the client idiomatic. But wait — the acceptance command is `python3 -m unittest tests.test_bench_client -v`, which runs my test loader. If I register in sys.modules there, it works. Let me do that. But to be safe and match the house pattern, let me check: the house pattern (test_instruments._load_offload_batch) does NOT register. To be consistent AND correct, I should register. Let me update my loader to register the module.\n\nActually, the most robust approach: register the module in sys.modules in the loader. Let me update _load_client. This is the recommended importlib pattern anyway.\n\nLet me update the test loader:\n```python\ndef _load_client():\n    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\"fn_stream_client\", CLIENT_PATH)\n    mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\n    sys.modules[spec.name] = mod\n    spec.loader.exec_module(mod)\n    return mod\n```\n\nNeed `import sys` in the test. Let me add it.\n\nAlternatively, I could avoid dataclasses. But dataclasses are idiomatic and the client is correct; the loader just needs to register. Let me go with registering in the loader — it's the correct importlib usage.\n\nLet me update the test file.\n\nActually, let me reconsider: is it better to make the client not depend on sys.modules registration? A dataclass defined in a module loaded via importlib without registration fails on Python 3.14. This is a real robustness concern. But the client's primary use is as a script. For test-loading, registering is standard. I'll register in the loader. That's the accepted fix.\n\nLet me update the test loader and add `import sys`.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"The dataclass needs the module registered in `sys.modules` when loaded via importlib on Python 3.14. Let me register it in the loader (the standard importlib pattern).\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_ac1c86e45cf045188f73fd41","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/70bb1f7ebb6a/bench-harness/tests/test_bench_client.py","edits":[{"oldText":"import importlib.util\nimport pathlib\nimport unittest","newText":"import importlib.util\nimport pathlib\nimport sys\nimport unittest"},{"oldText":"def _load_client():\n    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\"fn_stream_client\", CLIENT_PATH)\n    mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\n    spec.loader.exec_module(mod)\n    return mod","newText":"def _load_client():\n    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\"fn_stream_client\", CLIENT_PATH)\n    mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\n    # Register before exec so dataclasses/typing can resolve the module (py3.14).\n    sys.modules[spec.name] = mod\n    spec.loader.exec_module(mod)\n    return mod"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":1386,"output":1019,"cacheRead":95232,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":723,"totalTokens":97637,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787991031797,"responseId":"chatcmpl-452d450a-47a8-48a0-ab4b-33921c15f922","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_ac1c86e45cf045188f73fd41","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced 2 block(s) in /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/70bb1f7ebb6a/bench-harness/tests/test_bench_client.py."}],"details":{"diff":"     ...\n  13 \"\"\"\n  14 \n  15 import importlib.util\n  16 import pathlib\n+ 17 import sys\n  17 import unittest\n  18 \n  19 ROOT = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\n  20 CLIENT_PATH = ROOT / \"bench\" / \"fn-stream-client.py\"\n     ...\n  22 \n  23 def _load_client():\n  24     spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\"fn_stream_client\", CLIENT_PATH)\n  25     mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\n+ 27     # Register before exec so dataclasses/typing can resolve the module (py3.14).\n+ 28     sys.modules[spec.name] = mod\n  26     spec.loader.exec_module(mod)\n  27     return mod\n  28 \n  29 \n     ...","patch":"--- /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/70bb1f7ebb6a/bench-harness/tests/test_bench_client.py\n+++ /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/70bb1f7ebb6a/bench-harness/tests/test_bench_client.py\n@@ -13,8 +13,9 @@\n \"\"\"\n \n import importlib.util\n import pathlib\n+import sys\n import unittest\n \n ROOT = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\n CLIENT_PATH = ROOT / \"bench\" / \"fn-stream-client.py\"\n@@ -22,8 +23,10 @@\n \n def _load_client():\n     spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\"fn_stream_client\", CLIENT_PATH)\n     mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\n+    # Register before exec so dataclasses/typing can resolve the module (py3.14).\n+    sys.modules[spec.name] = mod\n     spec.loader.exec_module(mod)\n     return mod\n \n \n","firstChangedLine":17},"isError":false,"timestamp":1787991054101}]}
