{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The median reduction is working. However, my synthetic data has an issue: the reason every cell is \"divergent\" is that the fingerprints differ between req 0 and 1 (they're keyed by req). In the actual harness, every request within a load at the same depth uses the same prompt with greedy sampling, so all requests within the same load should produce the same fingerprint. The divergence across loads is what matters.\n\nIn other words, my synthetic generator has made fingerprints that differ between request indices, which is not representative — the real client gives the same fingerprint to all requests within a load (since they have the same prompt). Therefore, the \"divergent\" count of 2 for the stable cell is merely an artifact of the fact that my fake data gives different fingerprints to req 0 and req 1.\n\nThis means the Phase B divergence detection is too sensitive: it flags any cell with more than 1 distinct fingerprint, but this includes legitimate per-request variance if requests are given different prompts. But in the actual harness, all requests within a load share the same prompt (same depth), so they should have identical fingerprints. Therefore, if there's more than 1 distinct fingerprint within a cell, that's genuine divergence. My synthetic data simply isn't representative.\n\nLet me reconsider: does the actual client issue the same prompt to every request within a load? Yes — run_concurrent uses the same `prompt` for all requests. And greedy temperature 0. So all requests within a load produce identical output → identical fingerprint. Therefore, the fingerprint set for a cell (arm, depth) spanning 3 loads × N requests should be exactly 1 if deterministic, and more than 1 if divergent. Good — the logic is correct for real data.\n\nHowever, my synthetic test gave different fingerprints per request, triggering false \"divergence.\" This is a problem with the synthetic data, not with the logic. Let me fix the synthetic data so that requests within a load share fingerprints (keyed only by arm, depth, load — not by req). That way, the stable cell will have 1 distinct fingerprint and the divergent cell (spec-on/10240, varying per load) will have 3.\n\nLet me regenerate so that fp is keyed by (arm, depth, load) and not by req. Then:\n- spec-off/*: identical across loads → 1 distinct → not divergent.\n- spec-on/0: identical across loads → 1 distinct → not divergent.\n- spec-on/10240: varies per load → 3 distinct → divergent.\n\nLet me redo it. This will let us verify the correct behavior: only spec-on/10240 is divergent.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"The median reduction works, but my synthetic fingerprints varied per-request, which isn't representative — in the real harness every request in a load shares one prompt (greedy), so all requests in a load share a fingerprint. Let me regenerate faithfully so only the across-load divergence shows.\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_ceb0fff8ec1a488aa7b445e2","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/70bb1f7ebb6a/bench-harness\npython3 - <<'GEN'\nimport csv, hashlib\nFIELDS = [\"arm\",\"load\",\"depth_target\",\"depth_actual\",\"concurrency\",\"request_index\",\n          \"ttft_s\",\"queue_wait_s\",\"prefill_s\",\"decode_s\",\"total_s\",\"completion_tokens\",\n          \"fingerprint\",\"spec_config\"]\ndef fp(arm, depth, load):\n    # Same prompt per load -> same fingerprint for every request in a load.\n    key = f\"{arm}:{depth}\"\n    if arm==\"spec-on\" and depth==10240:   # this cell diverges across loads\n        key += f\":load{load}\"\n    return hashlib.sha256(key.encode()).hexdigest()[:16]\nrows=[]\nfor arm,spec in ((\"spec-off\",\"spec-off\"),(\"spec-on\",\"spec-on\")):\n    for load in (1,2,3):\n        for depth in (0,10240):\n            for req in (0,1):\n                rows.append({\n                    \"arm\":arm,\"load\":load,\"depth_target\":depth,\"depth_actual\":depth+10,\n                    \"concurrency\":4,\"request_index\":req,\n                    \"ttft_s\":f\"{0.5+req*0.01:.6f}\",\"queue_wait_s\":\"0.200000\",\"prefill_s\":\"0.050000\",\n                    \"decode_s\":\"1.100000\",\"total_s\":\"1.600000\",\"completion_tokens\":128,\n                    \"fingerprint\":fp(arm,depth,load),\"spec_config\":spec,\n                })\nwith open(\"/tmp/benchtest/matrix.csv\",\"w\") as f:\n    f.write(\"# fn-stream-client CSV — column semantics (synthetic test)\\n\")\n    w=csv.DictWriter(f, fieldnames=FIELDS); w.writeheader()\n    for r in rows: w.writerow(r)\nprint(\"wrote\", len(rows), \"rows\")\nGEN\necho \"=== Phase B ===\"\nMATRIX_CSV=/tmp/benchtest/matrix.csv MEDIANS_CSV=/tmp/benchtest/medians.csv DIVERGENT_CSV=/tmp/benchtest/divergent.txt python3 /tmp/rm_block_0.py\necho \"--- medians.csv ---\"; cat /tmp/benchtest/medians.csv\necho \"--- divergent.txt ---\"; cat /tmp/benchtest/divergent.txt"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":2470,"output":1221,"cacheRead":116736,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":571,"totalTokens":120427,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787991472145,"responseId":"chatcmpl-1f7bbae9-5a80-4531-a953-4496c41a0561","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_ceb0fff8ec1a488aa7b445e2","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"wrote 24 rows\n=== Phase B ===\nrun-matrix: reduced 24 rows into 4 (arm,depth) cells; 1 divergent\n--- medians.csv ---\narm,depth_target,concurrency,n_requests,median_ttft_s,median_queue_wait_s,median_prefill_s,median_decode_s,median_total_s,distinct_fingerprints,suspect\r\nspec-off,0,4,6,0.505,0.2,0.05,1.1,1.6,1,no\r\nspec-off,10240,4,6,0.505,0.2,0.05,1.1,1.6,1,no\r\nspec-on,0,4,6,0.505,0.2,0.05,1.1,1.6,1,no\r\nspec-on,10240,4,6,0.505,0.2,0.05,1.1,1.6,3,yes\r\n--- divergent.txt ---\nspec-on\t10240\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787991499784}]}
