{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Excellent! Phase D works perfectly. The receipt:\n- spec-on/10240 correctly flagged as divergent, suspect, qsa_signature=true (divergent at concurrency>1 with clean serial replay), serial_clean=true.\n- Other cells clean.\n- loads_per_arm=3, counterbalanced=true.\n\nNow let me verify this receipt passes the receipts-verify `_bench` gate. The gate checks:\n```python\ndef _bench(d):\n    if d.get(\"loads_per_arm\", 0) < 3: return \"fewer than 3 loads per arm\"\n    if not d.get(\"counterbalanced\", False): return \"arms were not counterbalanced\"\n    return None\n```\nMy receipt has loads_per_arm=3, counterbalanced=true. And step=\"bench\" starts with \"bench\". status=\"pass\". So it passes. Let me verify by copying the receipt to a temp receipts dir and running receipts-verify against it — but receipts-verify reads the real results/receipts. Let me just verify the _bench logic manually, or temporarily test. Actually, I already know it passes from reading the code. But let me do a quick sanity check by running receipts-verify's _bench on this data.\n\nActually, let me just confirm the gate logic accepts it by importing receipts-verify and calling _bench. Let me do a quick check.\n\nLet me also reconsider one thing: the receipt's `data.fingerprints` — the task says the receipt should be `{loads_per_arm, counterbalanced:true, arms, fingerprints}`. I have all of those: loads_per_arm, counterbalanced, arms, fingerprints. Plus extra protocol info (depth_series, concurrency, schedule, suspect_cells, etc.), which is good (\"every number carries its protocol\"). The receipts gate only checks loads_per_arm and counterbalanced. \n\nNow, let me verify the _bench gate accepts this exact data.\n"}}
{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"Phase D works end-to-end: `spec-on/10240` is flagged `divergent`, `suspect`, and `qsa_signature: true` (concurrent divergence + clean serial replay) while clean cells stay clean. Let me confirm this receipt passes the actual `_bench` gate in `receipts-verify.py`.\n\n"}}
{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":2,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_d2a6fa2dce954efda271155a","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/70bb1f7ebb6a/bench-harness\npython3 - <<'CHECK'\nimport importlib.util, json\nspec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\"rv\", \"scripts/receipts-verify.py\")\nrv = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec); spec.loader.exec_module(rv)\nreceipt = json.load(open(\"/tmp/benchtest/receipts/bench.json\"))\nerr = rv._bench(receipt[\"data\"])\nprint(\"step:\", receipt[\"step\"], \"| status:\", receipt[\"status\"])\nprint(\"_bench gate verdict:\", \"PASS\" if err is None else f\"FAIL: {err}\")\n# also confirm step prefix matches the BOUNDS routing\nprint(\"routed to _bench:\", str(receipt[\"step\"]).startswith(\"bench\"))\nCHECK"}}}}
