{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The receipt passes the `_bench` gate.\n\nNow let me also test the client's CSV writing and the actual client logic in a more integrated way — I can test the pure functions (parse_metrics, split_first_token, fingerprint_of, write_csv, fmt) and also test `write_csv` to ensure the header comment + DictWriter works. Let me also test that the client's main() argparse works (--help) and that build_parser doesn't error. And test write_csv produces the expected output.\n\nLet me also test the client against a local mock HTTP server to exercise the streaming + metrics path end-to-end. That would be a strong validation that the client actually works (SSE parsing, metrics scraping, concurrency, CSV output). Let me build a tiny mock server that:\n- Serves /v1/completions with streaming SSE (a few tokens + usage).\n- Serves /metrics with the queue/prefill/ttft histograms.\n\nThen run the client against it and check the CSV output + stdout JSON.\n\nThis is valuable because the acceptance only does py_compile, but I want confidence the client actually runs. Let me do this integration test in /tmp (not committing it).\n\nLet me write a mock server using http.server.\n\nThe client:\n1. converge_prompt: if depth>0, probes /v1/completions (non-stream) to get prompt_tokens. My mock should handle non-stream too. For depth=0, no probe. Let me test depth=0 first (no calibration), then depth>0.\n2. scrape_metrics before → GET /metrics.\n3. run_concurrent → POST /v1/completions with stream=true, logprobs=1.\n4. scrape_metrics after.\n5. split, CSV, stdout JSON.\n\nMock server behavior:\n- POST /v1/completions:\n  - Parse body. If stream=true: emit SSE chunks. Include logprobs with tokens and token_ids (to exercise the id path). Emit usage in final chunk (include_usage). Send [DONE].\n  - If stream=false (probe): return JSON with usage.prompt_tokens.\n- GET /metrics: return Prometheus text. To simulate deltas between before/after scrapes, the server should increment the histogram sums/counts on each completion it serves. So the before scrape has baseline, and after scrape has baseline + N requests' worth. Let me make the server stateful: track cumulative queue_sum, queue_count, prefill_sum, prefill_count, ttft_sum, ttft_count, and add a fixed amount per completion served.\n\nLet me implement: each completion served adds queue 0.5s, prefill 0.1s, ttft 0.6s to the respective sums and +1 to counts. Then before scrape (baseline) reflects completions served so far (calibration probes), after scrape reflects + measured batch. The delta = measured batch. For a batch of `requests` completions, queue_wait = 0.5, prefill = 0.1. Good — the client should report queue_wait_s=0.5, prefill_s=0.1.\n\nLet me write the mock and run the client at concurrency=2, requests=4, depth=0.\n\nI need to make sure the SSE format matches what the client parses. Client reads lines starting with \"data:\", parses JSON, looks at chunk[\"usage\"] and chunk[\"choices\"][].logprobs.tokens / token_ids. Let me emit choices with logprobs.tokens=[\" tok\"] and token_ids=[42].\n\nLet me write the mock server in /tmp and run the client via subprocess with --api pointing at it.\n\nLet me build it.\n\nActually, the client uses `urllib.request.urlopen` for streaming and iterates `for raw in resp`. For an HTTP response to be iterable line-by-line and for the server to stream, I need the server to flush each chunk. With http.server, I can write chunks and flush. Let me use BaseHTTPRequestHandler and write SSE lines with flush. But urllib may buffer. Let me set the response with no content-length and stream. Actually, for streaming, I should NOT set Content-Length; I'll send headers with Connection close and write incrementally. urllib's HTTPResponse iterates by reading; line iteration on a streaming response should work as data arrives if the server flushes. There can be buffering issues, but for a test it should be OK since the server writes all data then closes.\n\nActually, to keep it simple and robust, let me have the mock write all SSE chunks (with small flushes) then close the connection. The client iterates lines until [DONE] or EOF. Since the server sends everything and closes, the client reads all lines. Even if buffered, once the connection closes, all data is available. Good.\n\nLet me write the mock server as a background process, run the client, then kill it.\n\nLet me implement carefully. I'll use threading HTTP server.\n\nLet me write the mock server file and a runner.\n\nFor token_ids: I'll include \"token_ids\":[42,43] style. Actually each chunk one token. Let me emit 3 chunks each with one token, then a usage chunk, then [DONE].\n\nLet me also handle the probe (non-stream) for depth>0. Let me test depth=0 first (no probe), then optionally depth=64.\n\nLet me write it.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"The receipt passes the graded `_bench` gate. Now let me do a real integration test: run the actual client against a mock vLLM server (streaming SSE + `/metrics`) to prove the measurement path works end-to-end, not just compiles.\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_495488ee993c4185aba6465b","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"\"\"\"Mock vLLM server for integration-testing bench/fn-stream-client.py.\"\"\"\nimport json, threading\nfrom http.server import BaseHTTPRequestHandler, ThreadingHTTPServer\n\n# cumulative histogram state; each served completion adds fixed amounts.\nstate = {\"lock\": threading.Lock(),\n         \"queue_sum\": 10.0, \"queue_count\": 20,\n         \"prefill_sum\": 2.0, \"prefill_count\": 20,\n         \"ttft_sum\": 12.0, \"ttft_count\": 20,\n         \"completions\": 0}\nPER_REQ = {\"queue\": 0.5, \"prefill\": 0.1, \"ttft\": 0.6}\n\ndef metrics_text():\n    with state[\"lock\"]:\n        q, p, t = state[\"queue_sum\"], state[\"prefill_sum\"], state[\"ttft_sum\"]\n        qc, pc, tc = state[\"queue_count\"], state[\"prefill_count\"], state[\"ttft_count\"]\n    def hist(name, s, c):\n        return (f\"# TYPE {name} histogram\\n\"\n                f'{name}_bucket{{le=\"0.5\"}} {c}\\n'\n                f'{name}_sum {s}\\n{name}_count {c}\\n')\n    return (hist(\"vllm:request_queue_time_seconds\", q, qc)\n            + hist(\"vllm:request_prefill_time_seconds\", p, pc)\n            + hist(\"vllm:time_to_first_token_seconds\", t, tc)\n            + \"# TYPE vllm:num_requests_running gauge\\n\"\n              \"vllm:num_requests_running 1.0\\n\")\n\nclass H(BaseHTTPRequestHandler):\n    def log_message(self, *a):\n        pass\n\n    def do_GET(self):\n        if self.path == \"/metrics\":\n            body = metrics_text().encode()\n            self.send_response(200)\n            self.send_header(\"Content-Type\", \"text/plain\")\n            self.send_header(\"Content-Length\", str(len(body)))\n            self.end_headers()\n            self.wfile.write(body)\n        elif self.path == \"/v1/models\":\n            body = json.dumps({\"data\": [{\"id\": \"flashnext\"}]}).encode()\n            self.send_response(200)\n            self.send_header(\"Content-Type\", \"application/json\")\n            self.send_header(\"Content-Length\", str(len(body)))\n            self.end_headers()\n            self.wfile.write(body)\n        else:\n            self.send_response(404); self.end_headers()\n\n    def do_POST(self):\n        if self.path != \"/v1/completions\":\n            self.send_response(404); self.end_headers(); return\n        n = int(self.headers.get(\"Content-Length\", 0))\n        body = json.loads(self.rfile.read(n) or b\"{}\")\n        prompt_tokens = max(1, len(str(body.get(\"prompt\", \"\"))) // 4)\n        if not body.get(\"stream\"):\n            with state[\"lock\"]:\n                state[\"queue_sum\"] += PER_REQ[\"queue\"]; state[\"queue_count\"] += 1\n                state[\"prefill_sum\"] += PER_REQ[\"prefill\"]; state[\"prefill_count\"] += 1\n                state[\"ttft_sum\"] += PER_REQ[\"ttft\"]; state[\"ttft_count\"] += 1\n                state[\"completions\"] += 1\n            resp = {\"choices\": [{\"text\": \"ok\"}],\n                    \"usage\": {\"prompt_tokens\": prompt_tokens,\n                              \"completion_tokens\": 1}}\n            data = json.dumps(resp).encode()\n            self.send_response(200)\n            self.send_header(\"Content-Type\", \"application/json\")\n            self.send_header(\"Content-Length\", str(len(data)))\n            self.end_headers()\n            self.wfile.write(data)\n            return\n        # streaming SSE\n        self.send_response(200)\n        self.send_header(\"Content-Type\", \"text/event-stream\")\n        self.end_headers()\n        with state[\"lock\"]:\n            state[\"queue_sum\"] += PER_REQ[\"queue\"]; state[\"queue_count\"] += 1\n            state[\"prefill_sum\"] += PER_REQ[\"prefill\"]; state[\"prefill_count\"] += 1\n            state[\"ttft_sum\"] += PER_REQ[\"ttft\"]; state[\"ttft_count\"] += 1\n            state[\"completions\"] += 1\n        comp = 0\n        for i, (tok, tid) in enumerate([(\" Hello\", 101), (\" world\", 102), (\" now\", 103)]):\n            comp += 1\n            chunk = {\"id\": \"x\", \"object\": \"text_completion\",\n                     \"choices\": [{\"index\": 0, \"text\": tok,\n                                  \"logprobs\": {\"tokens\": [tok], \"token_ids\": [tid]},\n                                  \"finish_reason\": None}]}\n            self.wfile.write(f\"data: {json.dumps(chunk)}\\n\\n\".encode())\n            self.wfile.flush()\n        if body.get(\"stream_options\", {}).get(\"include_usage\"):\n            usage_chunk = {\"id\": \"x\", \"object\": \"text_completion\", \"choices\": [],\n                           \"usage\": {\"prompt_tokens\": prompt_tokens,\n                                     \"completion_tokens\": comp}}\n            self.wfile.write(f\"data: {json.dumps(usage_chunk)}\\n\\n\".encode())\n            self.wfile.flush()\n        self.wfile.write(b\"data: [DONE]\\n\\n\"); self.wfile.flush()\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    srv = ThreadingHTTPServer((\"127.0.0.1\", 8931), H)\n    srv.serve_forever()\n","path":"/tmp/mock_vllm.py"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":913,"output":2497,"cacheRead":122496,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1143,"totalTokens":125906,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787991540022,"responseId":"chatcmpl-9f2ff421-e541-46f5-af97-113dc0e101a7","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_495488ee993c4185aba6465b","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 4625 bytes to /tmp/mock_vllm.py"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787991592426}]}
