{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now, let's start the mock server in the background, run the client against it, and verify the CSV output and the JSON on standard output.\n\nLet's first test with depth=0, concurrency=2, requests=4. The client should report queue_wait_s=0.5, prefill_s=0.1 (from PER_REQ), and separate these from ttft.\n\nWait — let's think about the delta. Baseline state: queue_sum=10.0, queue_count=20. Each completion adds 0.5/1. With requests=4, the batch adds 4 completions → queue_sum +2.0, count +4. Before scrape: baseline (10.0, 20). After scrape: (12.0, 24). Delta: sum=2.0, count=4 → mean 0.5. Good. prefill: baseline (2.0,20), after adds 4×0.1=0.4 → (2.4,24), delta 0.4/4=0.1. Good.\n\nBut wait: converge_prompt only probes when depth>0. With depth=0, no probe. So before scrape = baseline. Good. With concurrency=2, requests=4, the batch serves 4 completions. Good.\n\nLet's run it.\n\nOne concern: the client's run_concurrent launches `concurrency` threads, and each processes its own slice. requests=4, concurrency=2 → chunks: idx0→worker0, idx1→worker1, idx2→worker0, idx3→worker1. So worker0 handles idx 0,2 and worker1 handles 1,3. Each worker processes 2 requests sequentially. Total 4 completions. Good.\n\nLet's run the client. We need to set the environment variable or pass --api http://127.0.0.1:8931, --metrics http://127.0.0.1:8931/metrics.\n\nLet's start the server, wait a bit, run the client, capture the output, then kill the server.\n\nLet's also test with depth>0 to exercise converge_prompt. Let's do depth=0 first, then depth=64.\n\nLet's run it.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_add6dd113a424fd9a11777e8","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/70bb1f7ebb6a/bench-harness\npython3 /tmp/mock_vllm.py >/tmp/mock.log 2>&1 &\nMOCK_PID=$!\nsleep 1\nrm -f /tmp/benchtest/client.csv\necho \"=== depth=0, concurrency=2, requests=4 ===\"\npython3 bench/fn-stream-client.py \\\n  --api http://127.0.0.1:8931 --metrics http://127.0.0.1:8931/metrics \\\n  --model flashnext --arm spec-off --load 1 --depth 0 \\\n  --concurrency 2 --requests 4 --max-tokens 16 --spec-label spec-off \\\n  --csv /tmp/benchtest/client.csv\necho \"=== client.csv ===\"; cat /tmp/benchtest/client.csv\nkill $MOCK_PID 2>/dev/null; wait $MOCK_PID 2>/dev/null\necho \"(mock stopped)\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":3440,"output":761,"cacheRead":122496,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":495,"totalTokens":126697,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787991592433,"responseId":"chatcmpl-309838ee-703b-47d3-b9ed-b68ec1447f77","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_add6dd113a424fd9a11777e8","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"=== depth=0, concurrency=2, requests=4 ===\n{\"arm\": \"spec-off\", \"load\": 1, \"depth_target\": 0, \"concurrency\": 2, \"requests\": 4, \"queue_wait_s\": 0.5, \"prefill_s\": 0.10000000000000009, \"prefill_source\": \"vllm:request_prefill_time_seconds\", \"queue_samples\": 4, \"prefill_samples\": 4, \"fingerprints\": [\"9052d965969e233b86b14d54d31c2bbeddb32ff0b833cc8146df7457b55a7240\", \"9052d965969e233b86b14d54d31c2bbeddb32ff0b833cc8146df7457b55a7240\", \"9052d965969e233b86b14d54d31c2bbeddb32ff0b833cc8146df7457b55a7240\", \"9052d965969e233b86b14d54d31c2bbeddb32ff0b833cc8146df7457b55a7240\"]}\n=== client.csv ===\n# fn-stream-client CSV — column semantics (spec claim 6.2; protocol per row).\n#   arm               bench arm label (spec-off / spec-on).\n#   load              load index within the arm, 1..loads_per_arm.\n#   depth_target      requested prompt depth in tokens (the independent var).\n#   depth_actual      prompt_tokens the server actually accepted.\n#   concurrency       number of in-flight sequences when this row was measured.\n#   request_index     per-request index within the load.\n#   ttft_s            CLIENT-side time-to-first-token: request release -> first\n#                     streamed token. Includes queue + prefill + first decode +\n#                     network + SSE framing. It is NOT prefill.\n#   queue_wait_s      SERVER-side scheduler queue wait, delta of the\n#                     vllm:request_queue_time_seconds histogram across this load's batch.\n#   prefill_s         SERVER-side prompt processing, delta of the\n#                     vllm:request_prefill_time_seconds histogram across this load's batch. Independent of\n#                     ttft_s: the reference harness duplicated ttft into this\n#                     column (evidence/nix-strix-halo.md §4.4); we do not.\n#   decode_s          CLIENT-side total minus ttft.\n#   total_s           CLIENT-side total request wall time.\n#   completion_tokens server-reported completion token count.\n#   fingerprint       sha256 over the completion's token ids (ints when the\n#                     engine provides them, token pieces otherwise).\n#   spec_config       speculative-decoding configuration active for the arm.\n# queue_wait_s and prefill_s are load-level server measurements shared by every\n# row of a load; ttft_s/total_s/decode_s/fingerprint are per-request.\n# Empty means \"the engine did not expose this metric\" — an honest absence.\narm,load,depth_target,depth_actual,concurrency,request_index,ttft_s,queue_wait_s,prefill_s,decode_s,total_s,completion_tokens,fingerprint,spec_config\r\nspec-off,1,0,10,2,0,0.000879,0.500000,0.100000,0.000576,0.001455,3,9052d965969e233b86b14d54d31c2bbeddb32ff0b833cc8146df7457b55a7240,spec-off\r\nspec-off,1,0,10,2,1,0.001044,0.500000,0.100000,0.000076,0.001120,3,9052d965969e233b86b14d54d31c2bbeddb32ff0b833cc8146df7457b55a7240,spec-off\r\nspec-off,1,0,10,2,2,0.000433,0.500000,0.100000,0.000361,0.000794,3,9052d965969e233b86b14d54d31c2bbeddb3