{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"The integration test works beautifully:\n- queue_wait_s = 0.5 (server-side, from metrics delta)\n- prefill_s = 0.1 (server-side, from metrics delta)\n- ttft_s = ~0.0008 (client-side, tiny because it's a local mock)\n- The three columns are distinct: ttft_s ≠ queue_wait_s ≠ prefill_s. This proves the separation and that prefill is NOT a duplicate of ttft.\n- Fingerprints are all identical (same prompt, greedy, deterministic) — good.\n- depth_actual = 10 (server-reported prompt_tokens).\n- concurrency=2 recorded per row.\n\nThe client works end-to-end. \n\nNow let me also test depth>0 to exercise converge_prompt. Let me run a quick depth=64 test. But the mock's prompt_tokens = len(prompt)//4, and converge_prompt will probe and rescale. Let me test it works without error.\n\nActually, let me verify converge_prompt works. With depth=64, the client probes. The mock returns prompt_tokens = len(prompt)//4. converge_prompt estimates reps to get ~64 tokens. It'll probe, get some count, rescale. This exercises the probe path. Let me test it doesn't crash and produces a reasonable depth_actual near 64.\n\nLet me run depth=64, requests=1, concurrency=1.\n\nActually, there's a subtlety: the probe requests (convergence) ALSO increment the mock's metrics (since they're completions). But the before-scrape happens AFTER convergence, so probes are in the baseline. Good. But let me verify the split still works (it should, since before-scrape is post-convergence).\n\nLet me run it."}}
{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"The three columns are genuinely distinct (ttft≈0.0008, queue=0.5, prefill=0.1) — the separation holds end-to-end, and fingerprints are deterministic. Let me also exercise the depth-convergence path (depth>0).\n\n"}}
