{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The integration test works beautifully:\n- queue_wait_s = 0.5 (server-side, from metrics delta)\n- prefill_s = 0.1 (server-side, from metrics delta)\n- ttft_s = ~0.0008 (client-side, tiny because it's a local mock)\n- The three columns are distinct: ttft_s ≠ queue_wait_s ≠ prefill_s. This proves the separation and that prefill is NOT a duplicate of ttft.\n- Fingerprints are all identical (same prompt, greedy, deterministic) — good.\n- depth_actual = 10 (server-reported prompt_tokens).\n- concurrency=2 recorded per row.\n\nThe client works end-to-end. \n\nNow let me also test depth>0 to exercise converge_prompt. Let me run a quick depth=64 test. But the mock's prompt_tokens = len(prompt)//4, and converge_prompt will probe and rescale. Let me test it works without error.\n\nActually, let me verify converge_prompt works. With depth=64, the client probes. The mock returns prompt_tokens = len(prompt)//4. converge_prompt estimates reps to get ~64 tokens. It'll probe, get some count, rescale. This exercises the probe path. Let me test it doesn't crash and produces a reasonable depth_actual near 64.\n\nLet me run depth=64, requests=1, concurrency=1.\n\nActually, there's a subtlety: the probe requests (convergence) ALSO increment the mock's metrics (since they're completions). But the before-scrape happens AFTER convergence, so probes are in the baseline. Good. But let me verify the split still works (it should, since before-scrape is post-convergence).\n\nLet me run it.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"The three columns are genuinely distinct (ttft≈0.0008, queue=0.5, prefill=0.1) — the separation holds end-to-end, and fingerprints are deterministic. Let me also exercise the depth-convergence path (depth>0).\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_d7704c9d00eb46d486b4cb6f","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/70bb1f7ebb6a/bench-harness\npython3 /tmp/mock_vllm.py >/tmp/mock.log 2>&1 &\nMOCK_PID=$!\nsleep 1\necho \"=== depth=64 (convergence), concurrency=1, requests=2 ===\"\npython3 bench/fn-stream-client.py \\\n  --api http://127.0.0.1:8931 --metrics http://127.0.0.1:8931/metrics \\\n  --model flashnext --arm spec-on --load 2 --depth 64 \\\n  --concurrency 1 --requests 2 --max-tokens 8 --spec-label spec-on \\\n  --csv /tmp/benchtest/client2.csv 2>&1\necho \"=== depth_actual + split columns (data rows only) ===\"\ngrep -v '^#' /tmp/benchtest/client2.csv | awk -F',' 'NR==1{for(i=1;i<=NF;i++)h[i]=$i;next}{print \"depth_target=\"$3\" depth_actual=\"$4\" queue=\"$8\" prefill=\"$9}'\nkill $MOCK_PID 2>/dev/null; wait $MOCK_PID 2>/dev/null\necho \"(mock stopped)\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":3087,"output":758,"cacheRead":124928,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":375,"totalTokens":128773,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787991611152,"responseId":"chatcmpl-f41f778e-788c-4726-8961-85d8ecacb74a","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_d7704c9d00eb46d486b4cb6f","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"=== depth=64 (convergence), concurrency=1, requests=2 ===\n{\"arm\": \"spec-on\", \"load\": 2, \"depth_target\": 64, \"concurrency\": 1, \"requests\": 2, \"queue_wait_s\": 0.5, \"prefill_s\": 0.10000000000000009, \"prefill_source\": \"vllm:request_prefill_time_seconds\", \"queue_samples\": 2, \"prefill_samples\": 2, \"fingerprints\": [\"9052d965969e233b86b14d54d31c2bbeddb32ff0b833cc8146df7457b55a7240\", \"9052d965969e233b86b14d54d31c2bbeddb32ff0b833cc8146df7457b55a7240\"]}\n=== depth_actual + split columns (data rows only) ===\ndepth_target=64 depth_actual=71 queue=0.500000 prefill=0.100000\ndepth_target=64 depth_actual=71 queue=0.500000 prefill=0.100000\n(mock stopped)\n"}],"isError":