, **never derived from the first-token series** — fixing the exact §4.4 defect where the reference harness shipped `prefill_mean_s == ttft_mean_s`.\n- Emits CSV with explicit column semantics in a header comment, a per-row concurrency field, and a **sha256 fingerprint of every completion's token ids**.\n\n**`bench/run-matrix.sh`** — the counterbalanced matrix:\n- Speculative on/off arms **interleaved A-B-B-A**, three loads per arm, medians, depth series **0 / 10240 / 102400**, rows under `results/`, and a receipts-gate-graded `bench.json` `{loads_per_arm, counterbalanced:true, arms, fingerprints}`.\n- Per the flashnext#4 steer: records per-row concurrency, and on fingerprint divergence across an arm's loads it **replays that arm serially (concurrency=1), byte-compares the token sequences via fingerprints, and flags the arm suspect** (QSA-gather signature recorded, not averaged over).\n\n**`tests/test_bench_client.py`** — feeds the client parser Prometheus fixtures with known queue and processing times and asserts the two columns separate them, plus a §4.4 regression guard that prefill is never the first-token column.\n\nVerification:\n- Exact acceptance argv passes (`py_compile` + `bash -n` + 10 tests OK).\n- Full suite green: **39 tests**, receipts-verify clean (no regressions).\n- Both embedded Python heredocs compile; the reduction + receipt logic was exercised end-to-end with synthetic data (correct divergence detection, suspect/qsa_signature flagging, and the receipt passes the graded `_bench` gate).\n- Integration-tested the client against a mock vLLM SSE+metrics server: ttft/queue/prefill come out as three genuinely distinct columns.\n- No banned model-family names, no GPL/secret material; commit touches only `bench/` and `tests/`.\n\nI did not push, merge, or read another task — those remain with the deterministic campaign nodes."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":1180,"output":781,"cacheRead":13